The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
owner = rq->hw_context->engine;
list_move(&rq->sched.link, pl);
```
Reason:
The bug occurs because when a virtual request is returned to its original virtual engine, its breadcrumb remains linked to the original physical engine. This can lead to a situation where the request completes in the background while the breadcrumb is still associated with the old engine, causing inconsistencies in request management.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
spin_lock(&rq->lock);
i915_request_cancel_breadcrumb(rq);
spin_unlock(&rq->lock);
```
Reason:
The fix involves decoupling the virtual breadcrumb from the original physical engine before moving the request back to the virtual engine. This ensures that the request does not complete in the background and attempt to cancel the breadcrumb on the virtual engine, thus preventing inconsistencies and potential errors in request management.

